      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not explicitly define “fine motor” as “finger-related sensorimotor skill” involving “precise” control of finger movements; it only references “finger sensorimotor skills (i.e., finger gnosis and fine motor skills)” and reports associations with numerical abilities, without giving that specific definitional phrasing.",
        "The second claim is supported: the packet states that reviewed studies evaluate the association between finger sensorimotor skills (including fine motor skills) and numerical abilities in children, and that fine motor skills predict multiple numerical measures."
